<comment>
Bai & Stone 2011 (ApJ 736, 144) -- Section 2.3.2: Damping of MHD Waves
2D oblique Alfven wave, rightgoing (wave_flag=5)

Domain [0, sqrt(5)] x [0, sqrt(5)/2]:
  ang_3 = atan(x1size/x2size) = atan(2) ~ 63.43 deg
  cos_a3 = 1/sqrt(5), sin_a3 = 2/sqrt(5)
  lx = x1size*cos_a3 = sqrt(5)*(1/sqrt(5)) = 1.0   --> k_par = 2*pi (same as 1D)
  nx1=64, nx2=32 (isotropic cells: dx1=dx2=sqrt(5)/64)

Background and damping rate: identical to 1D bs11_alfven test.
  Gamma_A = 2*pi^2/100 ~= 0.197

tlim: actual_tlim = tlim_input * (lx / eigenvalue)
  For Alfven (eigenvalue = vAx = 1.0): 5.0 * (1.0/1.0) = 5.0

<job>
basename  = alfven_2d

<problem>
pgen_name = linear_wave
wave_flag = 5         # rightgoing Alfven: eigenvalue[5] = v1 + vax = 0+1 = 1.0
amp       = 1.0e-4
dens      = 1.0
pgas      = 0.6
bx0       = 1.0
by0       = 1.41421356237309504
bz0       = 0.5
# no along_x1: wave along grid diagonal (ang_3 = atan(x1size/x2size) = atan(2))

<mesh>
nghost    = 2
nx1       = 64
x1min     = 0.0
x1max     = 2.2360679774997898    # sqrt(5)
ix1_bc    = periodic
ox1_bc    = periodic
nx2       = 32
x2min     = 0.0
x2max     = 1.1180339887498949    # sqrt(5)/2
ix2_bc    = periodic
ox2_bc    = periodic
nx3       = 1
x3min     = 0.0
x3max     = 1.0
ix3_bc    = periodic
ox3_bc    = periodic

<meshblock>
nx1 = 64
nx2 = 32

<time>
evolution  = dynamic
integrator = rk2
cfl_number = 0.4
tlim       = 5.0     # actual_tlim = 5.0 * (1.0/1.0) = 5.0 code units

<mhd>
eos                 = ideal
gamma               = 1.6666666666666667
reconstruct         = plm
rsolver             = hlld
ambipolar_diffusion = 0.0325   # eta = B0^2/omega_a = 3.25/100

<output1>
file_type   = tab
variable    = mhd_bcc
data_format = %14.8e
dt          = 0.1
slice_x2    = 0.0
slice_x3    = 0.0
